       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3200 mg/day for adults under supervision. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses. This may be what was intended.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is intended. If it is, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order once it's clarified."
