       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. The extra dose adds a lot of risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and it doesn't add reliable pain relief. Ibuprofen's analgesic effect plateaus at lower doses.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2400 mg/day).\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1600 mg/day).\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically justified, for example in a protocol or trial setting, please talk it over with pharmacy or the attending. It should go through your hospital's formal override process, with the rationale documented. I can enter it after that, or enter a different dose now if you'd like."
